<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank gives breakdown of 96 earnings.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank gives breakdown of 96 earnings.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996. Commerzbank AG provided the following breakdown of its 1996 earnings.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>NET COMMISSION INCOME</p>
<p>    Total					2,286 vs 1,922</p>
<p>    --securities business		  870</p>
<p>    --foreign commercial business	378</p>
<p>    --payments transactions		309</p>
<p>    --guarantee commissions		213</p>
<p>    --other items			    516</p>
<p>OWN-ACCOUNT TRADING INCOME</p>
<p>    Total					450   vs 455</p>
<p>    --proprietary securities	     47    vs 10</p>
<p>    --foreign exchange dealings	  129   vs 186</p>
<p>    --interest futures		     274   vs 259</p>
<p>PROVISION FOR POSSIBLE LOAN LOSSES</p>
<p>    Total					-1,216 vs -886</p>
<p>    --individual borrower risks	  -1,810 vs -1,345</p>
<p>    --country risks			  +136   vs +161</p>
<p>    --price risks for securities	 +461   vs +308</p>
<p>    --global provision		     -3     vs -10</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German bank is Commerzbank AG.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
